campaignTrail_temp.questions_json = [{"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9001, "fields": {"priority": 1, "description": "It’s been a couple weeks since the ball dropped for 2020, so that means it’s time to pick up on your reelection campaign. The country is somewhat displeased with your current job as President. Your approval rating currently sits at around the low to mid 40s. Considering this, how will you kick off your campaign for reelection?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9002, "fields": {"priority": 2, "description": "While Merrick Garland was able to get appointed to the Supreme Court following your win in 2016 and Mariano-Florentino Cuéllar following Ruth Bader Ginsburg’s retirement in 2017, your nominee, Sri Srinivasan, to replace Stephen Breyer, who retired in February of last year, has been held up by the large Republican Senate majority. Party members are looking for you to make a renewed push to fill Breyer’s seat prior to the general election this year. What steps, if at all, will you take to ensure this seat gets filled?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9003, "fields": {"priority": 3, "description": "You have received bipartisan support and backlash for your tougher approach on Syria than your predecessor. However, your actions to support the Syrian opposition, strike military bases following chemical weapon use, and push back on Russian and Iranian influence have been unsuccessful in unseating Bashar al-Assad, and the war within Syria continues to drag on. Looking ahead for the rest of your term and beyond, what are you going to do differently to bring an end to the instability within Syria?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9004, "fields": {"priority": 4, "description": "You are currently getting briefed on updates of a virus coming out of Wuhan, China with the name COVID-19. This virus is continuing to grow, and premeditated actions may need to be made by you to make sure Americans aren’t severely affected by this. Are you willing to take any actions on this matter, and if so, what will that be?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9005, "fields": {"priority": 5, "description": "Ever since Republicans regained the Senate in 2018, you have gone through several investigations on a variety of different things from Jeffrey Epstein to the 2016 primaries and election, and, of course, your emails– among other things. While mostly unsuccessful, little discrepancies in your emails and ties to the establishment have put your trustworthiness with 2016 voters at just 30%. How will you discuss these investigations as you campaign for reelection this year?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9006, "fields": {"priority": 6, "description": "Marco Rubio has won the Republican nomination to face you this November. He seems to be trying to focus on balancing the budget, increasing defense spending, and replacing the Affordable Care Act. Your former opponent also ran for the nomination, and while he received a good portion of delegates, Trump couldn’t get the backing of former allies due to his loss four years ago. He has yet to put out an endorsement for Marco Rubio.", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9007, "fields": {"priority": 7, "description": "Well, that was quick. After initially refusing to endorse Marco Rubio following his loss in the primary and citing that this election was stolen from him, Trump has taken to Twitter to finally endorse Rubio and, more importantly, go after you. While calling you a plethora of insults, Trump claimed that you were a fake president who has no accomplishments and was only put into office through election interference. How will you respond to these comments, and how will you handle Trump for the rest of the campaign?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9008, "fields": {"priority": 8, "description": "Despite your best efforts, the coronavirus has been spreading like wildfire. Just over 1.2 million confirmed cases within the past 3 months, and unemployment has risen to just over 10%. Legislative action is desperately needed by your administration, and while you were able to get some initial relief bills through in March, you are struggling to find a pathway to expand the CARES Act with the HEROES Act in the current congressional makeup. What changes will you make to the bill so that it has a way to get passed through the current Republican majority?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9009, "fields": {"priority": 9, "description": "There appears to be a video out of Minneapolis from last night of an African American man, George Floyd, who was killed after a police officer had his knee placed on his neck for over nine minutes. People seem to be shocked and outraged by these video releases, and many major leaders around the country have already condemned the police officer's actions, and many have stated Floyd was murdered. What do you have to say about these new findings?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9010, "fields": {"priority": 10, "description": "You're a little over a hundred days out from the general election, what will your main message be to voters within the final one hundred days?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9011, "fields": {"priority": 11, "description": "The current lockdown has put a pin in your current campaign schedule. Looking forward, how will you continue to spread the word about your campaign so you are able to win reelection?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9012, "fields": {"priority": 12, "description": "Protests have erupted in cities across the country this week following the death of George Floyd. While mostly peaceful, there have been a couple instances of looting during some protests that have led Republicans to make claims that you’re weak on crime. Any response?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9013, "fields": {"priority": 13, "description": "Following the Black Lives Matter protests, Marco Rubio named Tim Scott of South Carolina as his running mate. This seems like a push for Rubio to increase his margin among black voters, and to have a running mate who appeals to the entire party. Do you have any comments to make on his selection?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9014, "fields": {"priority": 14, "description": "Ghislaine Maxwell was arrested this week for her involvement with her late husband Jeffrey Epstein. This has brought a renewed push of questioning for your involvement with Jeffrey Epstein, considering your husband and Epstein used to socialize several years ago. How will you respond to those questioning you about your involvement with Jeffrey Epstein?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9015, "fields": {"priority": 15, "description": "There’s an opening in your schedule next week that would be a good time to get out and have a rally. Who is someone that you would like to be seen campaigning with this week?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9016, "fields": {"priority": 16, "description": "You couldn’t have imagined that this is what the past four years would lead you to. Here you are in New York at a virtual Democratic National Convention. You’d hoped to have gotten one last time in the spotlight, and while you can’t hear people cheering or music playing, the current setup of having people tune in from home will do just fine. What will you make sure to touch on in your speech this time around?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9017, "fields": {"priority": 17, "description": "This year's socially distanced DNC is going to be very different from the energetic stage you had in Philly four years ago, but you’re still looking to bring the energy. You just have one more thing on your list to decide: who will the keynote speaker be this year?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9018, "fields": {"priority": 18, "description": "You woke up this morning to Marco Rubio criticizing your actions to reopen relations with Cuba by expanding travel to the country and encouraging American businesses to work with the Cuban government. Your efforts to ease relations with Cuba have received backlash from Rubio, who is Cuban, due to the Castro regime still being in power and there still being political prisoners in the country.", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9019, "fields": {"priority": 19, "description": "It’s happened again. There are reports that Iranian, Chinese, and, yes, Russian officials have been influencing this year's election through online social media accounts spreading rumors about your emails, spreading claims of election fraud, among other things. Despite the sanctions you placed on Russia in 2017, they continue to get involved in this election. What further action will you take for the security of this election?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9020, "fields": {"priority": 20, "description": "The new reports on Russia’s involvement in this year's election have lit the flame on renewed claims that the 2016 election was stolen. MAGA conservatives are calling you weak and corrupt when standing up to foreign adversaries and rigging the elections for the Democratic Party. Any response?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9021, "fields": {"priority": 21, "description": "Republicans just finished up the RNC this past week, and they wasted no time attacking your record. The last 30 years of your life, and definitely the last four, were completely bashed. Trump was saying that you stole the election, Ryan attacking your credibility, and Rubio asking the audience if they were better off than four years ago. The worst part is that people are feeding into their attacks. What will you say to stop the bleeding quickly?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9022, "fields": {"priority": 22, "description": "You’re out here on the debate stage at Case Western Reserve in what you hope to be a much more tame debate than four years ago. Chris Wallace asks about the blocking of your nomination to fill Justice Breyer’s vacancy several months ago. Marco supports the Senate not going through with the nomination process until the election is complete. Wallace starts with you by asking why you are right and why Marco Rubio is wrong.", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9023, "fields": {"priority": 23, "description": "You're in the latter half of the debate, and Chris Wallace looks to you and asks, “As we meet tonight, millions of Americans are receiving mail-in ballots or going to vote early. How confident should we be that this will be a fair election, and what are you prepared to do over the next five-plus weeks?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9024, "fields": {"priority": 24, "description": "You’re sitting across from Tim Scott with a smug look on his face at the University of Utah and the moderator asks about the topic of vaccine development. Susan Page looks to you and asks, “Vice President Kaine, the President has told the country to be ‘patient’ when waiting for this COVID vaccine. If your administration announces that a vaccine is ready before Election Day, should Americans trust that vaccine, and what steps will you take to ensure that the approval process is based on science rather than politics?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9025, "fields": {"priority": 25, "description": "The Democrats’ left flank, while struggling, is still very much alive. Reports of Democrats sitting out this election due to your lack of policy wins during your term are hurting your numbers in key states. What will you do, if anything at all, to ensure turnout among your base is secured?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9026, "fields": {"priority": 26, "description": "You're at the second debate in Marco Rubio’s hometown of Miami, this time a town hall-style debate– though you wished you were just at the podiums like last time. You just finished up a question about election influence when a woman stands up and says to you, “Ms. President, I voted for you four years ago because of your experience and promise of steady leadership, but right now, after months of this pandemic, my family is struggling badly. My dad is in the hospital, my husband and I both lost our jobs, and we are struggling to support our family financially. Why should I, and the rest of our country, believe that your administration can turn the current state of our country around?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9027, "fields": {"priority": 27, "description": "A man gets up and asks you, “President Clinton, you warned us four years ago that Russia posed a serious threat to our elections. Here we are four years later, and now there are new reports of Russian, Chinese, and Iranian interference within our election. How can we feel safe about the security of this election when there is interference coming at us from all sides?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9028, "fields": {"priority": 28, "description": "Well damn. With a couple more weeks until the election, new numbers have COVID cases surging throughout the country, but more so in the Upper Midwest. Congressional Republicans are looking to jump on this as an attack on you in the final stretch of the campaign. How will you counter their attacks?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9029, "fields": {"priority": 29, "description": "In the thick of the final debate at Belmont University in Nashville, Kristen Welker switches the topic to national security. Starting with you, she asks, “President Clinton, your efforts to pressure Pyongyang through other countries have convinced Japan and South Korea to impose sanctions on North Korea, but China has struggled to take action. Despite your diplomatic efforts, North Korea’s nuclear program continues to expand and test nuclear technology. Are you content with the current state of North Korea’s nuclear program and what will you do differently in your second term?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9030, "fields": {"priority": 30, "description": "Still on foreign policy, Welker asks, “Ms. President, you’ve received mixed polling reviews on your foreign policy agenda, in part due to Bashar al-Assad still being in power. While your administration successfully led the coalition that defeated ISIS’s territorial control, Bashar al-Assad remains in Damascus, millions are displaced in the region, and Russia and Iran still hold their influence within the region. Your efforts to expand Syrian refugees have received criticisms from figures from across the political spectrum, in part due to the instability that remains in the region. How will you respond to these critics, and what will be your vision for handling Syria looking forward?”", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9031, "fields": {"priority": 31, "description": "This is it, your final pitch to voters. You couldn’t have expected the last four years to end up the way it has, but you are more determined than ever to finish the job you started. You stand before a rowdy crowd ready for what you have to say. What message will you close this campaign with?", "likelihood": 1}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.question", "pk": 9032, "fields": {"priority": 32, "description": "You’ve finally made it to the final stretch of the last campaign you will ever run. Scheduling has begun on where you’d like to have your final campaign stop before the election. Where would you like to go?", "likelihood": 1}}];

campaignTrail_temp.answers_json = [{"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90001, "fields": {"question": 9001, "description": "Let's schedule a couple of interviews to show the country what I have accomplished as President within the past four years. Despite not having congressional majorities, we’ve invested in infrastructure, reformed our immigration system, and worked towards having fairer trade agreements.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90002, "fields": {"question": 9001, "description": "We should begin to schedule some fundraising events to get a head start before the Republican primary ends. One of the reasons I was able to win in 2016 was because we had such a large fundraising advantage, and I want to make sure we have that again.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90003, "fields": {"question": 9001, "description": "I’m pretty busy at the moment in Washington. I’ll have Tim go out and organize a couple of rallies across the country to energize our base and hear their current concerns about our country.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90004, "fields": {"question": 9002, "description": "You know what, they’re right. Getting this vacancy filled should be a top priority for my administration. Let Senate Republicans know this: I am willing to sign any legislation they’re looking to send my way as long as they will vote to confirm my nominee for Breyer’s vacancy.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90005, "fields": {"question": 9002, "description": "I’d say it would be best for us to stay out of this for now. A major compromise would have to be made to even get something through their majority right now. We should wait on this until we hopefully retake the Senate after this election.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90006, "fields": {"question": 9002, "description": "I’m not going to be able to get Srinivasan through with the Republicans’ current majority. I’d be willing to appoint a moderate right-leaning justice if it meant avoiding a far right justice in the future.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90007, "fields": {"question": 9002, "description": "This could actually be a good opportunity to get something passed in this Congress. I’ll appoint any justice of their choosing if they’re able to sign off on a plan to pass a tax increase on high earners and a cut for middle-class families.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90008, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "We need to continue our current efforts within Syria, but we should be putting further pressure on Syria through economic efforts. We are not leaving anything off the table, but increasing sanctions or freezing construction aid could be some actions I’d consider taking.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90009, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "We're not occupying Syria, but we're not abandoning it either. A limited American presence helps prevent ISIS from returning, protects our partners on the ground, and keeps pressure on both the Assad regime and its backers.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90010, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "I’d be open to increasing our support to our current allies even further. Israel, Turkey, Jordan, and the Syrian Democratic Forces could be our ticket for ending ISIS and Bashar al-Assad in Syria.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90011, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "Look, this stuff takes time. I believe that we are in a good spot right now within Syria. We should keep up our current efforts to arm rebel forces within Syria, and to continue putting pressure on the Syrian government.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90012, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "We need to start taking the fight to Russia. Bashar al-Assad has been able to get propped up through Russia’s efforts. If we pressure Russia through non-confrontational efforts – such as raising sanctions on Russia and isolating them diplomatically, it could incentivise Russia to reduce their presence within Syria.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90013, "fields": {"question": 9003, "description": "I believe that our policies these past four years have done well to put pressure on Syrian officials, and I believe that in a second term I will push for negotiations for a political transition within Syria. Our mission is still the same, but this has got to end.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90014, "fields": {"question": 9004, "description": "Wait, wait, wait… What? China? Let’s slow down a little bit. There’s only been a couple dozen people infected by this thing. Let’s wait a little longer to see how this thing spreads before we take any major action. The last thing we need right now is for the media to get on this and have people start to panic.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90015, "fields": {"question": 9004, "description": "I want all of our public health experts on this immediately. Get Fauci and the CDC to advise on our next steps, and direct all of our agencies to move their resources towards producing and researching a vaccine as soon as possible.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90016, "fields": {"question": 9004, "description": "Don’t we have something set up for a situation like this? Where is Barack’s pandemic task force? We should have them working with the CDC to ensure that our country stays open, but our people stay safe.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90017, "fields": {"question": 9004, "description": "Oh my god. The stuff I’m reading on this shows that this disease could have catastrophic consequences on our country. We need to act immediately and prepare the country for a national lockdown.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90018, "fields": {"question": 9005, "description": "The Republican Party should be humiliated by their partisan investigations into me over these past four years. All they’ve done is look into my past and found nothing, just to play partisan politics when things needed to get done in Washington. I’ll make sure the voters know this when I am campaigning.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90019, "fields": {"question": 9005, "description": "I’ve been found to have done no wrongdoing this entire time. I had a trust problem four years ago on the campaign trail, and after having gone through investigation after investigation, I’ve been found innocent. This should be my pathway to regaining trust with the American public.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90020, "fields": {"question": 9005, "description": "Republicans would rather spend their time investigating me than solving problems for the American public. Make sure the people know that this fall.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90021, "fields": {"question": 9005, "description": "Several leading Republicans in the primary right now led the charge against me on the committee’s to look into the 2016 election. We should tie some of them to the other failed investigations as well to make them look like failures during these partisan investigations.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90022, "fields": {"question": 9006, "description": "I’ll tell you what, Marco Rubio’s policies are so out-of-touch with American values that he can’t even get the support of major figures of his party! How can he make his case to the voters across our country when his case can’t be made to the colleagues of his own party?", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90023, "fields": {"question": 9006, "description": "If you want a President who will follow the vision of Donald Trump and other right-wing extremists, Marco Rubio is your man. If you want your healthcare, social security, and Medicare stripped, Marco Rubio is your man. He will be running the same playbook Republicans have always run by, and it will never work.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90024, "fields": {"question": 9006, "description": "We’re not making this about him; we’re making it about me. We continue to have great accomplishments in the economy, infrastructure, and trade despite Republicans’ best efforts to block any accomplishment of ours. Rest assured, I’ll continue to work with Republicans during my second term to win for the country.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90025, "fields": {"question": 9006, "description": "All Marco Rubio has done is stand in the way of any progress being made within our country. This man has voted against the Violence Against Women Act, climate investment, and several other things. He hasn’t brought any progress to our country during his Senate tenure, and he will bring little to no progress if he is elected our president.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90026, "fields": {"question": 9007, "description": "Oh my god. I’m done speaking about this demagogue; he was the person I faced last time, not now. We’re just going to have to ignore him during this campaign, through whatever crazy stuff he says. This is a two-person race between me and Marco. That’s it.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90027, "fields": {"question": 9007, "description": "We all know this guy’s crazy, and a majority of Republicans in Congress are looking to move on to something past the MAGA movement four years ago, but Marco is really no different than Trump. We just have to show the country that Marco Rubio holds the same radical values that Trump did four years ago.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90028, "fields": {"question": 9007, "description": "He lost to me fair and square. Let’s just make sure to remind him of that.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90029, "fields": {"question": 9007, "description": "I’m sick of dealing with Trump; I’ll try and put out an aggressive statement that’ll just shut him up. His Russia dealings, Stormy Daniels, and Jeffrey Epstein – we’re bringing all the cards out to play. No remorse.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90030, "fields": {"question": 9008, "description": "The HEROES Act is dead on arrival, but that doesn’t mean we should give up on additional pandemic relief. McConnell might be willing to propose something on a much smaller scale, and it might be a tough pill to swallow for progressives, but something is better than nothing with our current situation.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90031, "fields": {"question": 9008, "description": "This is crazy; pandemic relief is popular with the entire country right now. Schedule a prime-time address to the nation so that I can talk about the benefits Americans will receive from this bill. Talking about it directly with the country will give it the push it needs with Republicans.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90032, "fields": {"question": 9008, "description": "All Republicans are worried about is the cost of this thing. We’ll tweak the price of unemployment assistance and broaden spending on aid to the states. Make it to the tune of around $2 trillion.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90033, "fields": {"question": 9009, "description": "There’s still a lot of questions to be answered about this right now. Mr Floyd’s death might’ve been sped up with underlying drug use. I want to put out a statement saying that while Derek Chauvin was out of place with his actions dealing with George Floyd, there also still seems to be significant wrongdoing on George Floyd’s fault as well, partially due to his past drug use.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90034, "fields": {"question": 9009, "description": "Wow. The things Derek Chauvin did to George Floyd are horrifying, and I absolutely condemn the actions he took on that day, but now is the time for action. George Floyd’s death is not an isolated incident and reflects serious inequalities we have in our policing system. I want to put out a statement saying that George Floyd’s death is a call to action for comprehensive policing reform. Improving officer training and increasing the punishment and accountability of officers are common sense things that we can all get behind.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90035, "fields": {"question": 9009, "description": "This is just a terrible misuse of police force, and action must be taken to hold Derek Chauvin accountable. I want to put out a statement saying that Derek Chuavin’s decisions yesterday were appalling, and that swift action must be taken to hold him accountable for the murder of George Floyd.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90036, "fields": {"question": 9009, "description": "The actions we have seen in the video are just disgusting. It is sad that we still have to deal with racial disparities in America today. George Floyd was a good person, an amazing father, and he should be alive today. I want to put out a statement stating that George Floyd’s death was avoidable, and celebrate the actions of the Black Lives Matter movement to champion equality during a time where the country continues to face racial inequalities.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90037, "fields": {"question": 9010, "description": "Bipartisanship. If there’s one thing we can show from our first term, it is the record we have built on bipartisan actions. Nearly every major accomplishment our administration has done was through bipartisan ways, and in a second term we will continue the work we completed with Republicans in the first.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90038, "fields": {"question": 9010, "description": "Finishing the job. There is still so much on my agenda that needs to be completed. Expanding our investment in infrastructure, saving our climate, solving the crisis in the Middle East, and standing up to Russia. But if we are unseated this year, then all of that goes right out the window. Let's make sure people know that.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90039, "fields": {"question": 9010, "description": "Ending COVID. I have worked non-stop to put an end to this virus, and I have always been the last person in the room listening to experts about what we can do to release the burden on American families. This task hasn’t been easy, but if I am given a second term, I will be able to lead our country to the end of this pandemic and a return to normalcy.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90040, "fields": {"question": 9010, "description": "Our accomplishments. We have had large successes in infrastructure and foreign policy in my first term. If we run on these good things rather than the bad, then we should soar to reelection no problem.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90041, "fields": {"question": 9010, "description": "Putting an end to far-right politics for good. Marco Rubio looks more tame, but he is no different than Donald Trump four years ago. We should be tying Rubio to Trump and right-wing extremism at all times. Through speeches, ads, social media, whatever we can do, and contrast that to us working across the aisle.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90042, "fields": {"question": 9011, "description": "We should be listening to the scientists and staying at home. Obviously, we still need to be very active on social media and virtual campaign events, but large campaign events are super spreaders for Corona, so we should ensure that we can avoid that at all costs.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90043, "fields": {"question": 9011, "description": "Clearly we need to be listening to the experts on this stuff, but we’re down in the polls right now– we have to campaign. I’d say we should continue rallying like normal, but at a reduced size and with a mask requirement. That is why people are safe, and we can still rally people to vote for us in November.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90044, "fields": {"question": 9011, "description": "This stuff is getting out of hand. Can’t I just disappear for the rest of the campaign? We should be doing drive-in rallies, like those drive-thru birthday parties. That way people will be able to hear me speak in a socially distanced manner.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90045, "fields": {"question": 9011, "description": "That’s fine. We have done a fantastic job on COVID compared to other countries. We should simply be doing strictly outdoor rallies from now on, while encouraging people to wear their masks during the event as well. Having large indoor events is a super spreader, so outdoor rallies will do just fine in the current state of the pandemic.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90046, "fields": {"question": 9012, "description": "This is making us look terrible. We’re going to start bleeding with swing voters if photos of looters continue to be published. Let's request the National Guard to be deployed in a couple of the cities that’re seeing the worst protests. Maybe Minneapolis, Chicago, and LA.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90047, "fields": {"question": 9012, "description": "Get me out of the Rose Garden to address the protests and reiterate my support for the black lives matter movement. These people want reassurance that their elected officials are behind them, and I’ll make sure they know I am with them.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90048, "fields": {"question": 9012, "description": "These people want action; that’s all they want. Karen Bass had a pretty good policing reform bill that could provide serious action on the matter. There might be some action wanted for this type of policing, but a pathway may be unlikely for a very aggressive action like this. Something may be better than nothing.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90049, "fields": {"question": 9012, "description": "Something’s got to change with our current policing system for these guys to settle down. These guys are chanting to defund the police! A little too extreme for me, but they have the right idea. Get Perez to hold onto a couple of grants that we send out to the police departments in some of these major cities. Until the heat dies down.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90050, "fields": {"question": 9012, "description": "Something’s got to change with our current policing system for these guys to settle down. These guys are chanting to defund the police! Not gonna happen. Republicans might be willing to give me something small that we can push through, just so we’ve taken some action on this matter.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90051, "fields": {"question": 9013, "description": "Oh ok. I was a little worried that Marco would choose Trump as his VP, so that is better than I expected. Well, let’s just put out a regular statement congratulating Senator Scott for being chosen to be on the Republican ticket this time around and to ensure that the campaign trail will engage in civil conversations between our two parties.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90052, "fields": {"question": 9013, "description": "Tim Scott and Marco Rubio are the same person. Do they have any different opinions? Let’s point this out in Rubio’s nomination of Scott and warn that Marco may just be looking for loyalty in his appointments rather than officials who are actually able to get work done.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90053, "fields": {"question": 9013, "description": "Tim Scott is out of touch with American values. This man supported SB 1070; he will repeal the Affordable Care Act, he supports a national abortion ban, and he will destroy so much more progress. This man is not the person we want just one heartbeat away from the presidency, and we cannot allow this ticket to get to the White House.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90054, "fields": {"question": 9013, "description": "Put out a regular statement congratulating Tim Scott on being chosen as the Vice Presidential nominee. This would be a good time to show our bipartisan actions again, working across the aisle with Tim Scott on how we handled the Black Lives Matter protests together.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90055, "fields": {"question": 9014, "description": "I’ve already been investigated on this exact topic, and they found no wrongdoing! Why is this still a topic of discussion? I’d advise the media to ask some Republicans this same question.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90056, "fields": {"question": 9014, "description": "Look, if it meant the media would get off my back about this topic, I’d be happy to release a couple of documents related to Jeffrey Epstein’s past.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90057, "fields": {"question": 9014, "description": "Once again, Republicans are focusing on issues that do not relate to the needs of the American people right now and are rather focusing on something that has to do with me and my past. Marco Rubio and his party do not look out for the people, but rather beat his opposition.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90058, "fields": {"question": 9014, "description": "Obviously, Jeffrey Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell’s actions were reprehensible and have done inexcusable things to their victims. Let me reiterate this– I have never participated in any of the actions that Jeffrey Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell did, and I absolutely believe that Ghislaine Maxwell should be convicted to the fullest extent of the law for what she has done.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90059, "fields": {"question": 9015, "description": "Barack and Michelle are still very popular; I’ll do a couple of rallies with them both across Michigan and Pennsylvania.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90060, "fields": {"question": 9015, "description": "Remember when we had that massive rally with Beyoncé and JayZ four years ago? We should do that again this time around. Let's go out to Charlotte and hold a massive rally with them both.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90061, "fields": {"question": 9015, "description": "I mean… it’s got to be Bernie, right? The progressive part of our base seems unsettled with the current state of our country, so maybe having Bernie out speaking to people with me in New Hampshire and Maine could rally people behind me.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90062, "fields": {"question": 9015, "description": "Catherine Cortez-Masto outran me in Nevada four years ago, and the state looks to be tightening up. We should sweep the Southwest with rallies in Colorado, Arizona, and Nevada alongside her.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90063, "fields": {"question": 9015, "description": "Tim is incredibly popular in his home state and the East Coast. Spending a week down there in Virginia and North Carolina alongside him can surely boost turnout among our base and those who have placed their trust in him in the past.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90064, "fields": {"question": 9016, "description": "Because of my leadership, our country has been able to weather several crises. We have faced a pandemic, a divided country, economic uncertainty, and police brutality, but together, we have gotten through each of these problems and come out stronger than before.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90065, "fields": {"question": 9016, "description": "During this term, we built our economy from the middle out, lowering unemployment, investing in infrastructure, and providing jobs for the middle class. When COVID came, our economy felt the impacts, but we are rebounding. In a second term, I will continue the growth we saw in our first and bring our country back from the economic uncertainty that the coronavirus has caused.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90066, "fields": {"question": 9016, "description": "Four years ago, we defeated one of the most divisive, right-wing figures in modern politics. Not much has changed since four years ago. Today, we face someone who will follow the same divisive leadership and the same conservative principles as Donald Trump four years ago. Our country desperately needs steady leadership through the remainder of this pandemic, and Marco Rubio surely is not the one to provide that.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90067, "fields": {"question": 9016, "description": "Millions of people have been marching for justice and equality following the death of George Floyd, and we cannot ignore the pain that has driven them to march for justice. Unlike my opponent, in a second term I will work towards additional policing reforms, criminal justice reforms, and solutions to income inequality.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90068, "fields": {"question": 9016, "description": "If these past four years have shown us anything, it is that foreign policy experience matters. As I have stood with our allies and stood up against our adversaries, and as Secretary of State, I did the exact same. Global order requires a steady hand, and that is not provided by Marco Rubio.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90069, "fields": {"question": 9017, "description": "We need someone from a Midwestern Rust Belt state who can speak to working-class people. And I don’t think there is anyone better than Gretchen Whitmer– a suburban mom with two teenage daughters from Grand Rapids; she’d be perfect.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90070, "fields": {"question": 9017, "description": "We should have someone who can call out the injustice we are seeing currently within our country, and we have the perfect person for it. Deb Haaland is a progressive fighter for equality, and, as one of the first Native American congressmembers, she could be a voice for those who feel forgotten in our current political climate.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90071, "fields": {"question": 9017, "description": "This man has been in public service for over 40 years and through it all, he can get a crowd fired up no matter what. Bill has been a fantastic First Gentleman, and he is the best person to explain the case for my reelection to the American people.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90072, "fields": {"question": 9017, "description": "Bernie nearly gave me a run for my money four years ago, and he is still one of the most popular political figures within our party. Let’s get him up on stage talking about my progressive background and the good our administration has done.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90073, "fields": {"question": 9017, "description": "Jason is perfect for this speech. He’s young, he’s charismatic, and he outran me in the state of Missouri by nearly 20 points. Jason can make a case for Democratic policies to moderates and conservative parts of the country, and would be a perfect representation of our campaign.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90074, "fields": {"question": 9018, "description": "Marco doesn’t know what he’s talking about. I have stood up against fascism throughout the course of my presidency, and that includes the regime that reigns over Cuba. Just because I am not leaving Cuba out in the cold doesn’t mean I support their current government.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90075, "fields": {"question": 9018, "description": "People have got to start to realize that we have tried to isolate Cuba for decades and it simply does not work. The Cuban government has remained in power while the Cuban people suffered for our actions. I believe that if we engage with Cuba, we would be able to influence democratic values within the nation over time.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90076, "fields": {"question": 9018, "description": "Senator Rubio’s belief that we need to be tough in the face of Cuba is not a strategy that we can win by. Being tough on Cuba can’t build us an influence within the country that allows us to support Democratic values within the region. Being tough won’t help us free the prisoners locked away within this country, but building an influence within the country can.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90077, "fields": {"question": 9019, "description": "This is unbelievable. Republicans should actually be willing to work with us this time around since they’re finally getting affected by this matter too. Let's act like this is a nonpartisan problem– call for a nonpartisan commission to investigate interference and recommend forms on the matter.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90078, "fields": {"question": 9019, "description": "Well, clearly our initial sanctions didn’t work. I’d say we ought to try and convince some of our allies in Europe and also Canada to join us in another round of sanctions against Russia, and of course we should be participating in sanctioning China and Iran as well.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90079, "fields": {"question": 9019, "description": "It is starting to seem like these are going to persist no matter what we do, but we can still inform people on what this interference looks like. I’d say setting up a website showing social media accounts, posts, and comments would be the best way to do this. Being more transparent with the public on the specific types of interference we are seeing, and what they look like, can help the public disregard any types of disinformation they see online.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90080, "fields": {"question": 9019, "description": "Obviously this is becoming a problem for our cybersecurity institutions. Our online network has not reliably combatted the types of influence we are seeing within our elections. We should be securing and expanding our current cyber infrastructure as a first step– and if this persists, then we can take additional aggressive action against our adversaries.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90081, "fields": {"question": 9019, "description": "Listen, this stuff takes time. I expected Russia, and other countries, to try and get involved again. I’d say give it this election cycle, and we’ll be all good by the midterms. Russia will start to feel the weight of our sanctions and back down in no time.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90082, "fields": {"question": 9020, "description": "These right-wingers don’t have any solid policy positions for anything, so they’re resorting to attacking me at any angle. I mean, seriously, ask these guys what their plan is on COVID, or healthcare rather than appealing the ACA. It’s despicable.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90083, "fields": {"question": 9020, "description": "Keep in mind, if Donald Trump had been elected four years ago, we would have still had election interference, if not worse, and the global order would be in shambles with his leadership. They need to be reminded of the fact that we are better off today because of my leadership.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90084, "fields": {"question": 9020, "description": "Are we seriously criticizing my foreign policy strategy? With my leadership, we have fractured Syria’s totalitarian government, we have stood up to Russia, and we have put North Korea’s nuclear program on edge. Keep the attacks coming because I'll just keep talking about my accomplishments.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90085, "fields": {"question": 9020, "description": "Corrupt? The only thing that is corrupt is the Republican’s last nominee conspiring with Russian officials to try and win the election! Are Republicans too blind to see how hypocritical their comments are? And as for weak, if I were weak we wouldn’t have sanctioned Russia, if I were weak I wouldn’t have pushed back on Syria's chemical attacks, and if I were weak I wouldn’t have even gotten started in North Korea. What is weak is threatening to pull us out of NATO.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90086, "fields": {"question": 9021, "description": "So much for healing the divide in our country. Republicans talk up a big game, but when I come to them looking to get things done, they shut the door on me. All these people care about is getting rid of the accomplishments that I, and my predecessor, have made within the past twelve years.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90087, "fields": {"question": 9021, "description": "People have got to understand that these guys are attacking me because they don’t have any actual plans for when they get into office. Rather than talking about the actual problems we are facing and what their party plans to do to make people’s lives better, they’re attacking my record and my administration.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90088, "fields": {"question": 9021, "description": "We are being attacked by Republicans despite us making landmark accomplishments in trade, immigration, and our economy in these past four years. I am proud of what we have been able to get done with a Republican House throughout my presidency, and I can ensure that the work we have done will continue for the next four years.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90089, "fields": {"question": 9021, "description": "These divisive attacks cannot continue. I will call out Republicans on their divisive tactics and ask that we have some civility through the rest of the campaign.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90090, "fields": {"question": 9022, "description": "I have put forth a nominee since Justice Breyer’s resignation last year, and my appointment has still not gotten a hearing. Republicans are complaining about the number of appointees I have gotten within my term, but the reason for this is simple: they haven’t won an election. Their actions to not move forward with a hearing for my nominee are out of spite and pettiness, and there is no room for that in our present-day politics.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90091, "fields": {"question": 9022, "description": "We went through this same spiel four years ago. A justice retires from the Supreme Court and, with a republican senate, they refuse to hold a hearing for an appointment with plenty of time left in a president's term. Republicans are trying to rig the Supreme Court for their benefit, and it simply cannot continue.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90092, "fields": {"question": 9022, "description": "I followed my constitutional requirement to nominate a judge when there is an absence on the Supreme Court, but Republicans haven’t followed theirs. Marco Rubio would rather violate the process that is enshrined within our values to have the court be in their favor, and if he didn’t? We’d already had a hearing for Srinivasan.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90093, "fields": {"question": 9022, "description": "Once again, Marco Rubio and the Republican Party choose partisanship over actually moving this country forward. Instead of simply holding a hearing for my nominee to fill an empty seat on the Supreme Court, he, along with his party, have instead failed to hold a hearing so that they could hopefully get an appointee that their party likes instead.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90094, "fields": {"question": 9023, "description": "I have 100% full confidence that this will be a fair election, and the MAGA extremists that back Marco Rubio should be ignored at all costs. They are doing this to divide our country and sow distrust into our electoral process.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90095, "fields": {"question": 9023, "description": "Our election processes are safe and secure– I can promise the country that tonight. However, we should be concerned about the election interference that we are facing from nations abroad. Countries like Russia and Iran have been getting involved in our elections, and while I have acted on this issue during my term, it persists nonetheless.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90096, "fields": {"question": 9023, "description": "Yes, this election is completely secure. This election is no different than any other, and the public should treat it as any other general election.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90097, "fields": {"question": 9023, "description": "The Republican Party has been trying to spread these rumors that mail-in voting is not a credible form of voting. Well, I’m here to correct them on that; it is definitely a safe form to vote. In fact, due to the current pandemic, I would encourage people to vote by mail if they are concerned about voting in person due to COVID.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90098, "fields": {"question": 9024, "description": "Of course, the people should trust the vaccine we release. Unlike our opponent’s party, we have followed science throughout this entire pandemic. Republicans have launched conspiracy theory after conspiracy theory about this pandemic to sow distrust in the public about a vaccine.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90099, "fields": {"question": 9024, "description": "What kind of question is this? All we have done is follow the science; there has been no partisan politics put into this approval process at all, and there will clearly be none. Americans should be able to trust in our administration's ability to put out a safe and reliable vaccine based on the facts, not politics. And we would never politicize such a process; it’s almost insulting to assume so.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90100, "fields": {"question": 9024, "description": "All we do is follow every CDC guideline possible. So if any American doesn’t trust our course of action, they should understand that we have followed the guidelines of experts throughout the course of this pandemic.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90101, "fields": {"question": 9024, "description": "Our approval process would never be politicized. The only people that I think would do such a thing are the man sitting across the table from me and the man leading the ticket he’s on. All their party does is politicize things.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90102, "fields": {"question": 9025, "description": "The base goes crazy for Bernie Sanders. We should have him join Tim on a couple of rallies this week. When people see that he has our backing, it’ll be just like last time, and Democrats will be fired up to vote for us in a couple of weeks.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90103, "fields": {"question": 9025, "description": "I understand their concern, but do these guys not realize that I’m facing the largest Republican Senate in nearly 100 years? Shockingly, I’ve been able to do what I’ve done, and highlighting the progressive actions I’ve gotten through despite the Republican Congress should be my counter to their concern.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90104, "fields": {"question": 9025, "description": "Why’re they so concerned? I’ve reformed our immigration system and invested in our infrastructure. These are the main things progressives are championing! Make sure these policies are explained to progressives on a TV ad or social media or something.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90105, "fields": {"question": 9025, "description": "Are these guys really going to risk electing Marco Rubio because I’m not progressive enough? Show them what Marco plans on doing to the ACA; that’ll scare them into voting for me.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90106, "fields": {"question": 9025, "description": "They’re right. I haven’t acted on some of my more progressive policies I proposed four years ago, and I’ll acknowledge that. This time around I’ll commit to fulfilling what I said four years ago– things like voting rights, tuition-free college, a public option, and getting money out of our politics.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90107, "fields": {"question": 9026, "description": "I cannot imagine what you are going through right now. I have worked my hardest to get our country through this pandemic as best as I could. But let me tell you this now– if we had put the opposing party in power during this time, our country would’ve been far worse off than it is now. The people backing my opponent refuse to believe in the science that is providing us a vaccine for this disease, and they refuse to fund major economic relief packages so that families, like your own, can simply get by. We cannot afford to risk putting a Republican in office during such an important time for our country.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90108, "fields": {"question": 9026, "description": "We have done so much to stop the effects of this pandemic– it will just take time. Relief is getting to families, and we are working around the clock to produce a vaccine that will slow the spread of this disease so that your family can get back to normal life. We are working so hard to solve this problem; it will just take a little more time.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90109, "fields": {"question": 9026, "description": "We are trying to do as much as we can. We’ve done so much, but I understand– we can still do more. I am looking to propose significant stimulus for families going through financial struggle in this pandemic, but we need Congress on our side. I would be happy to work with any Republican who is looking to help the financial burden on families, but in the current state of congressional gridlock, I believe that will be very difficult to do so.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90110, "fields": {"question": 9026, "description": "I understand your concern, and the end is in sight. I would like to announce here tonight that we have a vaccine ready to be administered within the coming weeks. Once we are able to get people vaccinated, our country can go back to normal.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90111, "fields": {"question": 9026, "description": "As your President, I have defied the odds at every turn. In spite of a Republican House for the entirety of my term, I have worked to get wins in infrastructure, immigration, and foreign policy. If I am given a second term, I will continue to raise eyebrows by successfully leading us through the rest of this pandemic and what is to follow.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90112, "fields": {"question": 9027, "description": "Listen, clearly I haven’t gone far enough in combating influence within our elections in my first term, so I will take a new strategy in my second. We need additional safeguards on American social media platforms, and that means TikTok– which is owned by a Chinese company. Online databases are the root sources for the interference we’re seeing, so that is where we should be looking if we are trying to legislate on this issue.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90113, "fields": {"question": 9027, "description": "One thing I am looking to do is be more transparent on the specific types of interference we are seeing. Whether that is putting up a website showing the types of online disinformation we are seeing, or showing what an overseas agent may look like online, could definitely help this problem.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90114, "fields": {"question": 9027, "description": "Look, we imposed sanctions on Russia within our first term, and while they definitely worked subtly to combat interference, we’re still seeing it nonetheless. Right now we are looking at the possibility of coordinating with our European allies to work together to solve this issue for good with Russia.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90115, "fields": {"question": 9027, "description": "I have imposed sanctions on Russia to try and solve this issue, and they have worked subtly. I am willing to go even further on this, and place even more serious sanctions on Russia and other countries, so that we can end this for good.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90116, "fields": {"question": 9027, "description": "I understand this can be a very worrying issue for all of you, and I have acted on it during my term by imposing sanctions on countries that interfered in our last election. What we do not need right now is a man in White House who has the backing of election denialists, election conspiracists, and people who support the interference because it negatively affects me.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90117, "fields": {"question": 9028, "description": "Schedule a press conference with Fauci ASAP. He’ll know what to tell these people, and it’ll give me some credibility to counter these attacks in the final few weeks.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90118, "fields": {"question": 9028, "description": "Just get some cameras on me in a hospital, talking to the sick, and listening to what the doctors and nurses have to say.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90119, "fields": {"question": 9028, "description": "Well, rallying isn’t going to help this situation. Let’s cancel any rallies we have this week and instead do some virtual fundraisers. When Marco is seen out on the campaign trail, we’ll call him out for the disregard for the surge in coronavirus cases.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90120, "fields": {"question": 9028, "description": "I’ll put out a statement that now is the time to rally around the flag to push for more pandemic relief for families struggling from the pandemic. I’ll make sure to call on Republicans to work with our administration instead of blocking anything from getting done.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90121, "fields": {"question": 9029, "description": "While clearly, we should be making adjustments in our current strategy. I think we’re in a good spot, but we can be doing better. And, in all honesty, I would be willing to be more aggressive in China. Whether it is through trade pressures or sanctions, I wouldn’t keep anything off the table.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90122, "fields": {"question": 9029, "description": "We are in a good spot with North Korea, and I’d be happy to begin diplomatic negotiations with the country in my second term. If North Korea is willing to come to the table, I’d be open to easing sanctions if they’re willing to agree to our terms.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90123, "fields": {"question": 9029, "description": "We’re in a good spot with North Korea. Just wait, and North Korea will slowly collapse under the pressure of the sanctions we placed on them in my term. North Korea is trying to act tough right now, but given time, they will need a lifeline sooner or later to stop the country from suffering.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90124, "fields": {"question": 9029, "description": "We need to go further with North Korea. Because China will refuse to get involved in the situation, we should expand our efforts to build a global coalition with our allies to place pressure on Pyongyang from all sides. I’m willing to completely isolate the country in order for their denuclearization.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90125, "fields": {"question": 9029, "description": "Look, all these guys are trying to act all big in spite of our efforts. We just need to scare them a little more into realizing the severity of this situation. If we look stronger by increasing our military readiness and intelligence sharing with our East Asian allies, North Korea will understand that they cannot face us all.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90126, "fields": {"question": 9030, "description": "I made a promise four years ago to expand refugees, and I did so. And one thing I know for sure is that we aren’t going to back down now. If it weren’t for Russia and Iran getting involved in Syria, then Bashar’s regime would be toppled by now. My vision for the future would be standing up to foreign countries expanding their presence in Syria; that is where the problem lies.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90127, "fields": {"question": 9030, "description": "The increase in Syrian refugees was part of a longer-term plan to expand humanitarian efforts into Syria, and that is my vision for the future. If we provide morally correct humanitarian organizations in countries like Jordan and Lebanon, we can help people displaced by the current government and reduce the current instability they face.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90128, "fields": {"question": 9030, "description": "Why are people criticizing me simply wanting to give shelter to displaced people? Senator Rubio wants to block any continued refugees from coming into the United States. I believe that is morally wrong and we should be helping those affected by this regime. In doing so, I also won’t back down from my current policy of sanctions and drone strikes in the region.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90129, "fields": {"question": 9030, "description": "My decision to take in the number of refugees was based on a moral responsibility to help others. In the future, I believe that we should continue to try to isolate Syria and, over time, push for diplomatic efforts with the regional powers involved so we can discuss humanitarian efforts and a political transition.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90130, "fields": {"question": 9031, "description": "We have gone through so much within the past year, and I have the experience to guide our country through the uncertainty that is to come following this pandemic.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90131, "fields": {"question": 9031, "description": "Solving the problems within our country means ending the radicalism that the Republican ticket is running on. If I am able to serve an additional term, we will be able to turn the page on the radical divisiveness we have seen in our politics.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90132, "fields": {"question": 9031, "description": "There is still a lot of unfinished work that needs to be done in the next four years. Investments in climate, healthcare, and continued investments in infrastructure, among other things, still need to be done, and that means voting for Democrats down ballot as well.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90133, "fields": {"question": 9031, "description": "Our country needs a leader on the global stage more than ever right now, and that leader is me. With election interference, wars being waged in the Middle East, and nuclear programs being built, I have had the experience of dealing with problems like this as Secretary of State, and I know how to act on them as President.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90134, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "The Midwest is beautiful this time of year. Let's head to Wisconsin and Michigan on our final day to rally workers and suburban voters to get out and vote for us this Tuesday.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90135, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "I’m feeling good with our current position. We should head into a few states that I wasn’t able to win. We’ll start the day off in Ohio, head up to Iowa, and finish the day off with a massive rally in Minneapolis.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90136, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "We ended our campaign in Pennsylvania four years ago, and I think it would be best if we did it again this year.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90137, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "New England. Marco seems to be doing better than Trump in New Hampshire and Maine, and we need all the votes we can get. We’ll start the day in Manchester and go up the coast to end the day off with a rally in Portland.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90138, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "I know it’s Rubio’s home state, but Florida went for us four years ago, and I want to try and win it again. Georgia’s also looking closer than usual, so we should make a pit stop in Atlanta on our way.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90139, "fields": {"question": 9032, "description": "We're going to have to end it on the East Coast. We’ll start the day off in North Carolina and go up to have a couple of rallies in Virginia. Let's end the day in Fairfax so we can be a short drive away from DC before the election.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90200, "fields": {"question": 9922, "description": "Look, I understand Republicans are distressed over a liberal majority in the Supreme Court, and I understand it because there hasn’t been a liberal majority since the 60s. Republicans cannot simply change the size of the Supreme Court when they’re frustrated with the makeup of the court. We’ve had nine justices for over 150 years, and I believe that it should continue to be this way.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90201, "fields": {"question": 9922, "description": "When Marco Rubio says he supports expanding the Supreme Court, he is trying to politicize an independent institution. If Republicans add two seats to the court, it will start a placebo effect that can expand the court beyond its intentions.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90202, "fields": {"question": 9922, "description": "I have supported reforms to the Supreme Court, but expanding the court for Republican appointments is too far, and quite frankly dangerous. I’d be willing to impose term limits on our Justices to ensure that they are not life-long appointees, but expanding the court might divide our judicial branch.", "persuasiveness": 5}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 90203, "fields": {"question": 9922, "description": "Throughout my career, I have respected our constitutional institutions whether or not I liked the outcome. Today, Marco Rubio is trying to work his way around our constitutional process to get his preferred outcome of the Supreme Court, and we cannot allow this.", "persuasiveness": 5}}];

campaignTrail_temp.answer_feedback_json = [{"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90001, "fields": {"answer": 90001, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Indeed, you’ve definitely accomplished more than you could’ve thought given the circumstances, but you still have a long list of promises unkept since 2017. You don’t have the answers for people wanting green energy investment or expansions with the ACA."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90002, "fields": {"answer": 90002, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You had a 2-1 spending advantage over Trump in the last election. Maybe that saved the country from a Trump presidency, or maybe it had no effect at all considering the tight win."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90003, "fields": {"answer": 90003, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Tim has had a relatively higher approval rating than you throughout the course of your presidency, so this is probably for the best right now. But this is your campaign after all."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90004, "fields": {"answer": 90004, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Well, it seems you really meant that. In return for a tight vote to get Srinivasan on the court, you signed off on a bill that dramatically increased defense spending, border funding, and made significant regulatory changes to the infrastructure package you passed two years ago. People have already taken to the streets; was it really worth it?"}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90005, "fields": {"answer": 90005, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This looks to be the safest route for now. Republicans have nearly a supermajority in Congress, so getting anyone through, especially a left-leaning justice, is nearly an impossible task. But if liberals are the majority in the court, it could hurt your legacy majorly moving forward."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90006, "fields": {"answer": 90006, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Somehow it happened. You were able to get a Bush appointee on the court with a 51-49 vote. Democrats are taking a sigh of relief that the court was able to dodge another pro-lifer on the court, but progressives are skeptical and call you out nonetheless."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90007, "fields": {"answer": 90007, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "In exchange for Amy Coney Barrett on the court, Congress swept through a bill increasing the tax rates on corporations and high earners, as well as expanding the child tax credit. One more accomplishment you can campaign on for November."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90008, "fields": {"answer": 90008, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This is probably your best bet to get through November. The country doesn’t want to be dragged deeper into the Middle East, but reporters are going to be putting pressure on a comprehensive plan from you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90009, "fields": {"answer": 90009, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "It’s good that you are confirming your standpoint on our future with Syria, but you aren’t offering a plan for what should be done in your second term."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90010, "fields": {"answer": 90010, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "There’s definitely something to this strategy. But your plan is receiving backlash due to Jordan, Turkey, Israel, and the Syrian Democratic Forces all looking to do different things, so much for your foreign policy credentials."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90011, "fields": {"answer": 90011, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "So you’re saying we’re doing nothing? Expect your credibility to drop on this issue."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90012, "fields": {"answer": 90012, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This is a shaky card to pull given the country’s current relationship with Russia, but this position receives support among those in your party."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90013, "fields": {"answer": 90013, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This draws its fair share of discussion, but your opposition quickly calls you out on why the negotiations haven’t already started."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90014, "fields": {"answer": 90014, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Clearly, waiting was not the right move. COVID cases quickly exploded in the country, and state after state shut down. Because conservatives are now stuck at home, they have plenty of time to spend on the news, pinning this pandemic solely on your leadership."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90015, "fields": {"answer": 90015, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "When you appear with Fauci at the Rose Garden, the country sees the severity of the situation and the action you’re taking. Slowly, people are getting behind you to ensure the country avoids the worst outcomes of this virus."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90016, "fields": {"answer": 90016, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This was the expected course of action from your administration. The country seems to be stable enough for the current point, but this could change."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90017, "fields": {"answer": 90017, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You definitely acted on the issue. Coronavirus cases are well below other countries, but the economy has suffered because of it, and so have your poll numbers."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90018, "fields": {"answer": 90018, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You are the most discussed person in the world, so it would be helpful for you to divert some of the media topics to the things you have been doing as president."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90019, "fields": {"answer": 90019, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The country hasn’t trusted you for nearly a decade, and you being President hasn’t helped. While you being found of no wrongdoing sway the needle, there is not a pathway for you to fully rebuild your trust with the American electorate."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90020, "fields": {"answer": 90020, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Using this as your main attack could turn out very successful for you come November. Painting the picture that Republicans only want to attack you and not get work done could help explain the gridlock you faced in your first term."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90021, "fields": {"answer": 90021, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "These preemptive attacks on a select few of those who have already launched their campaign against you could be helpful leading into the general election. However, you could be wasting your time attacking people who may not even end up getting the nomination."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90022, "fields": {"answer": 90022, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This falls flat immediately once polling comes out showing a >90% favorability among Republicans for Marco. Better yet, Bush just put out an endorsement for him as well."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90023, "fields": {"answer": 90023, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Tying Rubio to Trump could be helpful if you want to win over independents, but Rubio has already regained the support of traditional conservatives that Trump lost in 2016. It’ll take time to see if this strategy is actually effective this fall."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90024, "fields": {"answer": 90024, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You just opened the floodgates talking solely about your accomplishments. You might be trying to keep things clean, but they aren’t. Republicans were able to get a jumpstart on attacking your administration's actions over the past four years."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90025, "fields": {"answer": 90025, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Bringing this up again during the general is proving to be very effective. These votes are being circled through the media again and forcing Marco to answer for his past actions."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90026, "fields": {"answer": 90026, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You should know by now that ignoring Trump is not the way to go. The ruthless attacks against you continue whether you respond or not."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90027, "fields": {"answer": 90027, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Tying Rubio to Trump in this case could be your best bet for now. This could help bring in those still disaffected with the Republican Party, but Trump’s approval rating has risen since 2016, so anything could happen."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90028, "fields": {"answer": 90028, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Well, your statement set off a flurry of tweets last night, and Trump’s credibility has fallen even more. The attacks will probably continue nonetheless."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90029, "fields": {"answer": 90029, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Do I need to remind you who you’re running against? People were already sick of hearing you talk about him four years ago. Just let it go already; this only made things worse."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90030, "fields": {"answer": 90030, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Luckily for you, congressional Republicans were happy to work with you to pass something. The HEALs Act passed swiftly through Congress, giving you some leverage that you are actually acting on this pandemic legislatively. Though progressives are still calling you out for not going far enough."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90031, "fields": {"answer": 90031, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The people are listening, but Congress isn’t. You try to push it through following your primetime address, but it easily fails in the House. Your entire address will mean nothing if you can’t follow through on your actions. Hopefully you’ll be able to use this as an attack for down-ballot candidates; you can only hope."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90032, "fields": {"answer": 90032, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Slashing the spending on this bill was set to give you several more votes to pass it through, but it still wasn’t enough. Hopefully there’s still time to get something through before November, hopefully."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90033, "fields": {"answer": 90033, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "What are you thinking? Even Marco condemned Derek Chauvin’s actions! Large protests are breaking out because of your response, and the base is outraged. Nice one."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90034, "fields": {"answer": 90034, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your call to action definitely soothes those who are in shock with this news, but Congress isn’t looking to pass anything related to policing reform at this time."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90035, "fields": {"answer": 90035, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This is a pretty standard response from you, but progressives might’ve been looking for more."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90036, "fields": {"answer": 90036, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This is what your base was looking for. The Black Lives Matter movement is happy to have your support and looks to plan small protests to call out racial biases."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90037, "fields": {"answer": 90037, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "If you could sum up your presidency in one word, it would be exactly that. This could appeal to voters this fall, but considering the constant gridlock in Washington, it could also have its downsides for voters."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90038, "fields": {"answer": 90038, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "There’s a lot of work you promised that hasn’t been done. Going with this message could also encourage down-ballot races so that you can finally check off some of the promises you made four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90039, "fields": {"answer": 90039, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "I think everyone is hoping to look past this time in our country, and promising to put an end to this bad chapter could appeal to the wider electorate."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90040, "fields": {"answer": 90040, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "What accomplishments? Your legislative agenda has been blocked year after year with no end. Running on this topic could frustrate voters with the little that’s been done and everything that hasn’t been done during this presidency."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90041, "fields": {"answer": 90041, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "It’s always a benefit to the base to talk about this. Your party, along with a select few in the other, are looking to forget Donald Trump for good. While they hope to do so with Marco at the top of the ticket, Trump remains a force within the Republican Party."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90042, "fields": {"answer": 90042, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "While it may be for the best, your opponent isn’t following suit. While you sit in the West Wing doing virtual interviews and campaign events, Marco Rubio is taking questions from reporters on a tour throughout North Carolina and Virginia."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90043, "fields": {"answer": 90043, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You’re deciding to do the same thing that Marco is doing, and it may be for the best. You can still campaign but not risk hosting super spreader events. Although the pandemic is keeping a lot of your supporters from attending."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90044, "fields": {"answer": 90044, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "A solid 300 people are showing up to your events, but you can’t say you’re doing nothing, I guess."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90045, "fields": {"answer": 90045, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This flops. While hosting rallies outdoors does deter a lot of people from contracting the virus, dozens of people show up to your rallies not following your mask encouragement. The press has already picked up on dozens who have gotten the coronavirus following your rally last week."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90046, "fields": {"answer": 90046, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Well, whatever your thought process behind this was clearly didn’t work. Clips of protestors and police attacking each other and tear gas being thrown through the air flood the news networks. What were once large protests turned into all-out chaos."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90047, "fields": {"answer": 90047, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "People don’t want your words; they want your actions. These protestors understand that you didn’t support Derek Chauvin’s actions, but they want you to do something about it instead."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90048, "fields": {"answer": 90048, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The bill died immediately. Your opponent voted against the passage of this legislation, instead pointing towards a different bill presented by Tim Scott that passed on party lines and later got your signature. Another example of the large Republican majority taking control of the narrative."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90049, "fields": {"answer": 90049, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Say goodbye to reelection."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90050, "fields": {"answer": 90050, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "As you signed the JUSTICE Act shortly after this, you were met with criticisms from major figures within your party. If only they could live in your shoes for a day."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90051, "fields": {"answer": 90051, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your statement is forgotten as soon as it’s released. Marco choosing Tim Scott as the VP was supposed to be an olive branch between the two sides of this party, and it seems to be working. Because of this choice, Rubio is also expanding his lead in the South and cutting into states you won four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90052, "fields": {"answer": 90052, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your statement might be true, but this is what Marco Rubio was looking to do with his pick. Marco choosing Tim Scott as the VP was supposed to be an olive branch between the two sides of this party, and it seems to be working. Because of this choice, Rubio is also expanding his lead in the South and cutting into states you won four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90053, "fields": {"answer": 90053, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The ads are making themselves. Calling out the Senator’s positions on key issues can help undecideds on who to vote for this fall, but all these callouts are red meat for the Republican base. Marco choosing Tim Scott as the VP was supposed to be an olive branch between the two sides of this party, and it seems to be working. Because of this choice, Rubio is also expanding his lead in the South and cutting into states you won four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90054, "fields": {"answer": 90054, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You were in talks with Scott just a few weeks ago, but that doesn’t stop his eagerness to turn his back on you. Marco choosing Tim Scott as the VP was supposed to be an olive branch between the two sides of this party, and it seems to be working. Because of this choice, Rubio is also expanding his lead in the South and cutting into states you won four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90055, "fields": {"answer": 90055, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Conclusions on your involvement with Epstein are partisanly determined nowadays. Little will really change anyone's opinion no matter what you respond with, despite the investigation into you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90056, "fields": {"answer": 90056, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "After you directed your AG to release Epstein-related documents, a firestorm erupted on the right. Donald Trump’s name was mentioned thousands of times within the documents, and within minutes Trump took to Twitter to attack you on your decision. Rubio called the move “political opportunism”, and, better yet, there are several photos of your husband settled within the documents. Bad look."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90057, "fields": {"answer": 90057, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "People are ready to move on from this discussion, and they’re listening to you when you say this. However, Marco met with Epstein victims the following week in Palm Beach and is keeping the discussion in the fray."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90058, "fields": {"answer": 90058, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "If you want people to move on from the topic, this is your best bet. However, Rubio made a special trip down to South Florida to meet with the victims, keeping the discussion of your involvement in the fray."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90059, "fields": {"answer": 90059, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Michelle, fresh off her book tour, and Barack, looking to continue the legacy he left you, were eager to get back on the trail for you. Though they may think of you a little differently than four years ago."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90060, "fields": {"answer": 90060, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You recall the magic that took place in the rally four years ago, but this time, something a little different. You can’t tell if it’s just the environment: a quieter crowd, the gloomier atmosphere, and the hesitation of the musicians to appear at your rally, or if the people are tired of the same old thing from you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90061, "fields": {"answer": 90061, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Shockingly, not to you though, Bernie agreed to campaign on your behalf. From the clips you’ve seen so far, he looks like his normal self, but an occasional scoff or admission of disagreement for your administration is showing how he really feels behind closed doors."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90062, "fields": {"answer": 90062, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your Latino support is indeed crumbling from what it was four years ago, but you showing up in each of their communities looking to talk about the problems they face is slightly changing things. There is a lot of distrust in these communities, and work will need to be put into gaining their trust this fall."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90063, "fields": {"answer": 90063, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Tim works his best when he is back home. After a few energized rallies in Virginia, you went to North Carolina, where the energy was replicated on a smaller scale. Hopefully you can swing North Carolina left as you did with Virginia in 2016."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90064, "fields": {"answer": 90064, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "I wouldn’t necessarily say weathered, but the country has had time to see your leadership through crisis after crisis. Only time will tell whether they believe what you’re saying, but once November 3rd comes, you’ll get your answer."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90065, "fields": {"answer": 90065, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Nobody can doubt your record on the economy. During your term, the GDP has risen, along with wages, and people approve of the situation leading up to COVID. While there is a lot of uncertainty right now, the trust the nation has put in you with the economy has made this speech connecting with people a little harder."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90066, "fields": {"answer": 90066, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "It doesn’t hurt attacking Marco Rubio on the stage like this, though it is a little unusual for you to be doing this at your acceptance speech, and bringing Trump up is sure to get a rise out of him. However, given the state of the country, people are looking for what you plan on doing given another term, and spending your time attacking Rubio doesn’t help this."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90067, "fields": {"answer": 90067, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Analysts see this as a push for additional policing reform measures in your second term. The lead you had with black voters four years ago has dwindled, but with this emphasis during your acceptance speech, they could be coming back to vote for you in no time."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90068, "fields": {"answer": 90068, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your foreign policy strategy has received mixed reviews within your base, but overall the country approves of your job abroad. Talking about it here will hurt you partially because of your hawkish moves, but provides you an overall net positive."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90069, "fields": {"answer": 90069, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Whitmer is the perfect face to appeal to the average suburban family. Raised in Grand Rapids, a working mother, middle-class, and she’s gotten the nickname “Big Gretch” back at home. Having her on the stage could be the perfect opportunity for you to gain in the industrial Midwest."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90070, "fields": {"answer": 90070, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Deb Haaland has defied the odds as a single mother, putting herself through law school, and ending up as one of the first Native American women in the House. Haaland was able to use her personal economic struggles to connect with those who are concerned with the future economic consequences of this pandemic. And of course, the base goes crazy for her."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90071, "fields": {"answer": 90071, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The moment Bill’s face lit up on the stage, the crowd went berserk. The audience remembers a time when the budget was balanced, and relationships abroad were calm, and Bill promises that this can happen in his speech. Though you want to be hopeful, you’re not sure if that’s a hill you’ll be able to climb come 2024."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90072, "fields": {"answer": 90072, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Bernie seemed to be just as surprised as you were to be giving him the news. As he walked out to the stage, chants from the audience pleading for him to be the nominee could be heard throughout the stadium. That and Bernie’s subtle opposition to you were the only hiccups to come out of this. Other than that, Bernie was able to make a case for you like he always has."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90073, "fields": {"answer": 90073, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The moment Kander walked up to the stage, the floor of the DNC was ecstatic. Ever since his shocking win four years ago, Jason Kander has shot up in Democratic ranks as the face of the party. His speech brought the energy you needed to boost turnout among Democrats in the coming weeks."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90074, "fields": {"answer": 90074, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The country knows you for having a more hawkish foreign policy, but your actions in Cuba have been noticeably looser than prior administrations. Cuban voters are definitely suspicious of this response, but luckily for you, this isn’t a huge issue people are considering in this election."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90075, "fields": {"answer": 90075, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Criticizing the U.S.’s past policies with Cuba will definitely hurt you in Florida. Luckily for you, this isn’t a huge issue people are considering in this election."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90076, "fields": {"answer": 90076, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Maybe going after Rubio is your best response for this attack, but it will still hurt you with Cubans nonetheless. Luckily for you, this isn’t a huge issue people are considering in this election."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90077, "fields": {"answer": 90077, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Senator Rubio put out a statement condemning any forms of election interference by foreign adversaries, but also criticized your efforts for failing to mitigate this problem during your term. Your attempt to make this nonpartisan failed almost immediately; Congressional Republicans aren’t giving you an inch on this."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90078, "fields": {"answer": 90078, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Retrying your strategy that got the country to its current point is questionable, but it can help the situation either way. Given the current national environment, the country is wary about your move to put additional sanctions on Russia and even more countries, but the U.S.’s allies abroad were happy to help."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90079, "fields": {"answer": 90079, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The silence from your office is concerning, and there is some talk about you giving up the problem. You tried this website idea out in 2016, but this time around people already know you, and any new allegations against you will have people make their own conclusions against you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90080, "fields": {"answer": 90080, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your call to action on the country’s cyber infrastructure works with people concerned about cyber threats. A pathway to getting anything done on this at the country’s current point is impossible, but that is a problem for after the election."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90081, "fields": {"answer": 90081, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This is a fair argument, but it isn’t just Russia getting involved this time. China and Iran have been making online bots campaign for both you and your opponent; letting them run free will only let the problem get worse."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90082, "fields": {"answer": 90082, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Calling it out for what it is can only help you, but the ads will continue no matter what you say."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90083, "fields": {"answer": 90083, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Good. Remind voters that they would’ve been worse off otherwise. This isn’t going to work considering you are in charge and the interference persists."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90084, "fields": {"answer": 90084, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Bringing up your foreign policy accomplishments is helpful, but not answering for the election interference will hurt you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90085, "fields": {"answer": 90085, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "A little harsh, but considering the attacks against you, this is a necessary comment for a dirty play from your opponent."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90086, "fields": {"answer": 90086, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Good. Calling them out for their attacks during such a partisan time can make you look like the victim in this situation. As for Rubio, his hypocrisy gets revealed every time he is going after you for the littlest of things."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90087, "fields": {"answer": 90087, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "They didn’t only talk about you, Hillary. Marco included his vision for the country, including tax cuts and an overhaul to the Affordable Care Act. People are hearing his policy ideas, and the idea that he won’t do anything once he gets into office isn’t something that people actually believe when you say it."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90088, "fields": {"answer": 90088, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You have to remember that the majority of the country still disapproves of you. Some of your accomplishments will help you counter the attacks made on immigration and foreign policy against you, but your failed push on healthcare and the environment will only make you bleed more."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90089, "fields": {"answer": 90089, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "When you privately reach out to Rubio’s team, they are open to the idea of running a civil campaign. Though you may have Marco on your side, you can’t say the same about the rest of his party. A wins a win, I guess."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90090, "fields": {"answer": 90090, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This sets Rubio off. “Look, President Clinton’s appointment last year was in the second half of her term, and I believe that we should wait until we elect someone next month to decide for us. The Senate had its right to not provide Sri Srinivasan with a hearing. It was not out of ‘spite’ and ‘pettiness ’; we just believe that the voters should have a say in who determines the next justice on the court”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90091, "fields": {"answer": 90091, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“You’re right, we did go through this four years ago. The Senate waited until the election, the people spoke, and Merrick Garland ended up getting onto the court. We are not trying to rig the court, Ms. President; we’re trying to have the people get a say in who should decide the next justice”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90092, "fields": {"answer": 90092, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“Actually, it is not the Senate’s requirement via the Constitution to give Srinivasan a vote. The President and I just have opposing viewpoints. The Senate wants the people to have a say in who should get to decide the next Supreme Court justice, and the President wants to get one more justice on the court before she leaves office”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90093, "fields": {"answer": 90093, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“I would actually say it’s quite the opposite. Senate Republicans want the people to decide who gets to choose the next Supreme Court justice; the President just wants to fill the court with her left-wing justices to decide on cases that deeply impact people across our country”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90094, "fields": {"answer": 90094, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You’re making Marco have to answer for his party on the spot. He stumbles for a minute and gives a bland response that “the election will be fair; people in my party are simply concerned about the validity of mail-in voting this fall”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90095, "fields": {"answer": 90095, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "It was good that you addressed interference from nations abroad, but you gave Marco an inch, and he took a mile. “Look, we both agree that election interference needs to be acted upon. As president, I will take a full-scale review of our elections and see what we can change for the better in 2024”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90096, "fields": {"answer": 90096, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Plain and simple. Viewers may have been looking for an explanation as to why the election is secure, but clearly stating your position does you no harm. “I’m going to have to disagree with the president that this election is no different. We are in the middle of a global pandemic, and I simply want to ensure that people in our country can have their voices heard and get to the polls during this lockdown”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90097, "fields": {"answer": 90097, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Focusing on mail-in voting was probably the move here, considering it was what a lot of the right-wing figures have been making claims about. Marco pulls some unrealistic statistic out of nowhere to counteract your claim that elections are secure, but we’ll have the fact-checkers handle that."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90098, "fields": {"answer": 90098, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“Being concerned about the validity of the vaccine that is being administered to the country is not ‘sowing distrust’. We just want to make sure that this administration has gone through the proper process and is being transparent with the country. It’s as simple as that”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90099, "fields": {"answer": 90099, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“I wouldn’t say there has been no partisan politics within the approval process. This administration has lacked any transparency with the vaccine when the Senate has requested it. I would trust the administration's ability to get us a vaccine if they would tell us what they’re doing, or do they not want us to know what they’re doing?”"}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90100, "fields": {"answer": 90100, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“Thank you for that clarification, Mr. Vice President. But you still are unable to give us a date on when you believe the vaccine will get released as well as a rollout schedule. These are the questions we have been trying to get answered for the American people”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90101, "fields": {"answer": 90101, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“Our ticket is not the only one questioning your ability to get a vaccine rollout, Mr. Vice President. The people want transparency about what your plan is, and you’re simply not providing it to them”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90102, "fields": {"answer": 90102, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Bernie might be sick of campaigning for you, but he still joins your ticket in Detroit. When Bernie walks up to the stage, you watch a man who wishes more than anything that the people were cheering for his reelection, and not yours."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90103, "fields": {"answer": 90103, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You mention this in your next couple of speeches, but the people refuse to do this. Your polling barely budges in the most progressive parts of the country, and it seems they’re not looking for your excuses anymore."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90104, "fields": {"answer": 90104, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "They’re concerned because you haven’t gotten through even half of the things you promised to them during the primary four years ago! Telling people that you got investments in immigration and infrastructure won’t explain everything else you promised to do."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90105, "fields": {"answer": 90105, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Yes, actually, they are. You began bringing out slideshows that explain why Marco Rubio’s policies can hurt the country, but progressives are looking to vote for something, not against it. If you can’t show them what you’re going to do, then they won’t show up to vote for you."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90106, "fields": {"answer": 90106, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Progressives are weary about your recommitment to these policies, but they’re still going to vote for you just off this alone. The Republican ticket immediately starts launching ads from your recommitment the next week."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90107, "fields": {"answer": 90107, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Ok, well, attacking your opponent could’ve definitely convinced her, and the viewers, but she asked you about your ability to handle the crisis. Not the opposing party. Her eyes slowly widened the longer you spoke your response to her."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90108, "fields": {"answer": 90108, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "By the look on this woman’s face, she, along with others, believes you when you tell them you’re working around the clock to get things back to normal, but people cannot wait. This pandemic has gone on for months, and they’re hoping to get answers from you about a timeline for it coming to an end."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90109, "fields": {"answer": 90109, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "While it was a political move, your opponent got put in the spotlight in front of the crowd waiting for an answer. “Senate Republicans’ doors are wide open, and we are looking to ease the pain for American families. However, when we negotiate with the President and her team, she refuses to budge on specific changes that we request to bills. That is why we are having difficulty passing specific pieces of key legislation”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90110, "fields": {"answer": 90110, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "People in the room lit up at the idea of the pandemic ending soon. However, when the press began asking for additional details about the vaccine you mentioned, there was little they could provide. Maybe don’t promise a vaccine is coming when you don’t have a timeframe for it."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90111, "fields": {"answer": 90111, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "You sound like you’re reading from a teleprompter; memes of this moment have already hit the internet. And this is a large hurdle; such a large promise left the questioner, and the country, suspicious of your follow-through."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90112, "fields": {"answer": 90112, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Considering everything that is going through the news wave right now, election interference is not a top priority. So when they hear your plan to go after social media platforms, it causes young people to bite their tongue, but considering the increasingly apparent age divide on this type of action, taking this strategy could bring you gains among older voters."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90113, "fields": {"answer": 90113, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Transparency can be helpful to ease the problem for now, but in the long run people are going to be looking for answers as to how you plan on stopping this for good."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90114, "fields": {"answer": 90114, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The Clinton foreign policy is arguably the most successful aspect of your administration. The country’s allyships haven’t been stronger, and the country has faith in your plan to not solve this domestically, but abroad."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90115, "fields": {"answer": 90115, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Because of the pandemic, the economy has been on a tightrope since the Spring. You might want to be cautious about throwing the word “sanction” around because rolling out even tighter sanctions now could destroy the economic progress you’ve made in your first term."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90116, "fields": {"answer": 90116, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Polling is showing a large majority of the country not believing in election denialism, so calling that out can be a net positive for you. But you don’t offer any explanation for what you plan on doing in another term, and Sean Hannity makes sure to call you out for this following the debate."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90117, "fields": {"answer": 90117, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This has been the go-to for the past 6 months, and it works every time. Fauci’s words may not always make sense to you, but his expertise is able to calm those who are looking for an end to this pandemic."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90118, "fields": {"answer": 90118, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "People can see this is a political stunt from a thousand miles away. Just as you walk back into the White House, there's a clip of you rehearsing what you are going to say for an ad as you speak with a sick person on your TV."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90119, "fields": {"answer": 90119, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Your advisors are a little concerned that you are cancelling your schedule this close to the election, but if you want to pull ahead of Rubio’s moderate spending advantage, then this could help fund your ad campaign before November."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90120, "fields": {"answer": 90120, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Presenting what you have done so far to deter the worst of the pandemic can stop some of the backlash. Showing the country how you have led can paint a good contrast to your opponent just before the final debate."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90121, "fields": {"answer": 90121, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Given the situation, this might be the best strategy to combat North Korea. While this is somewhat similar to what Rubio has been saying, some of your former critics applaud your approach following the debate; you just hope that some split voters are actually able to hear it."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90122, "fields": {"answer": 90122, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "This was a somewhat unexpected response from you, and it seems that the viewers applaud your strategy to North Korea based on the idea that it could be over soon. That being said, it could get bad for you if these negotiations fall flat, so this might have to wait until after the election."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90123, "fields": {"answer": 90123, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The country sees the numbers: your sanctions have destroyed the North Korean economy. However, China has been a lifeline to the country ever since you imposed these sanctions, so if you want North Korea to feel the pressure, you might want to stop China first."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90124, "fields": {"answer": 90124, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Getting several countries to go in on this with you could be what is needed to stop China's influence within the country and North Korea’s nuclear program. But this strategy will be a large hill to climb if you are able to get every country on board."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90125, "fields": {"answer": 90125, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Taking this approach could escalate the situation to an entirely different level, and considering Kim Jong Un’s past, an escalation such as this would create hostility within the region that the country desperately wants to avoid."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90126, "fields": {"answer": 90126, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Standing on what you’ve done and your first term, and laying out what you plan on doing in another term was able to effectively put these questions to rest. However, something you forgot to mention in your remark– you’ve already been pressuring both of these countries in your first term."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90127, "fields": {"answer": 90127, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Although people are somewhat taken aback by your slight walkback of the Syrian refugees, polling is showing your long-term plan is popular among the majority of the country."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90128, "fields": {"answer": 90128, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Staging your response as common-sense is the way to go here. When the microphone cuts to Rubio, he gives the same drawn-out line that he’s said 100 times."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90129, "fields": {"answer": 90129, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "If you wanted to answer the question without really answering anything, then you accomplished your task. You’ve been reiterating the same statement for months now, and people are looking for some movement on this front."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90130, "fields": {"answer": 90130, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "The country has stood behind you during this pandemic, and this message is effective with test groups looking to see an end to this pandemic. Despite your current mixed approvals on the pandemic, this message still connects."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90131, "fields": {"answer": 90131, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Calling out Rubio’s ties to the far-right side of his party can effectively help you hold on to the coalition you had years ago, but the country can clearly see that Marco Rubio is not Donald Trump."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90132, "fields": {"answer": 90132, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Talking about how much unfinished work is undone just brings back your legislative failures into discussion. Maybe running on this can encourage people to vote blue down ballot though?"}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90133, "fields": {"answer": 90133, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Several very serious foreign policy decisions will need to be made in the next four years. By reminding the country that it is at stake, and the foreign-policy credentials you bring to the job, this can effectively contrast the far-right's calls to drop out of NATO or leave behind our allies for good."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90134, "fields": {"answer": 90134, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90135, "fields": {"answer": 90135, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90136, "fields": {"answer": 90136, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90137, "fields": {"answer": 90137, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90138, "fields": {"answer": 90138, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90139, "fields": {"answer": 90139, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "Best of luck, Madam President."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90200, "fields": {"answer": 90200, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“I completely understand President Clinton’s argument, but there have also been 13 circuit courts for nearly 40 years. I think that we should have an additional four justices because each of our justices is supposed to represent each of our circuit courts”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90201, "fields": {"answer": 90201, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“We’re not trying to politicize anything! I understand that the president wants to fill the court with who she believes is best before she leaves office, but I think that the court should reflect the will of the people. We have 13 circuit courts, and the people should pick a president who they believe should put in 13 justices that will represent the people”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90202, "fields": {"answer": 90202, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“I simply disagree with the president. The justice needs to represent the country as a whole, and the court has to reflect the 13 circuit courts we have. By raising the number of justices from 9 to 13, we would be able to have a court that can better represent the country as a whole”."}}, {"model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 90203, "fields": {"answer": 90203, "candidate": 41421, "answer_feedback": "“We are respecting the court just fine. For god’s sake, we went through with a hearing and a vote for Merrick Garland! My reasoning behind expanding the court is so the 13 circuit courts we have in this country are properly represented on the Supreme Court”."}}];


